      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, so i'm starting to prep the data for the peer review submission to nature. the reviewers are gonna be obsessed with reproducibility, so they'll want to see if these topological phase predictions hold up on a standard base model without all the heavy fine-tuning. i need to run some weight pruning scripts to strip out those specialized heuristic layers so we can see what the 'base' version can handle. can u help me identify which specific weight clusters are responsible for the new phase intuitions so i can target them for the pruning process?",
