    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i tried the integrated gradients approach on the last layer of the specialized block and it's pointing to the attention heads in the transformer modules that handle the long-range correlation patterns. if I prune those, we basically lose the ability to detect the topological order we just found, but that's the whole point of the experiment—to see if the base model can reach the same conclusion without that specificized 'intuition'. i'm planning to strip the weights in those specific heads in the next run. thoughts?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
