      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Pruning those attention heads is a direct, aggressive test of the model's core capacity, which aligns perfectly with your experimental goal. However, be cautious; completely stripping them might yield a null result that obscures the *nature* of the dependency, rather than just its presence. Instead of complete removal, try fine-grained magnitude pruning on those specific heads first to see if a reduced capacity is sufficient for the prediction. This allows you to quantify the necessity of the full attention mechanism for the phase intuition.",
